# ─── Shipped Google OAuth credentials ──────────────────────────────────────
# Alfred ships with OAuth client credentials so users can "Sign in with Google"
# without pasting anything. These are read at BUILD TIME (Rust `option_env!`),
# baked into the binary.
#
# Setup (Google Cloud Console):
#   1. Create a project; enable "Google Calendar API" and "Gmail API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen (type External). Scopes:
#        .../auth/calendar.readonly, .../auth/gmail.readonly, openid, email, profile
#      While unverified, keep it in "Testing" mode and add your test users
#      (sensitive-scope verification by Google is required before public release).
#   3. Create an "OAuth client ID" of type "Desktop app".
#   4. Copy the Client ID + Client secret below.
#
# Provide them at build/run time. They are NOT auto-loaded — export or pass inline:
#   export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs) && npm run tauri:dev
#   # or:
#   ALFRED_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=... ALFRED_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=... npm run tauri:dev
#
# If left unset, the backend falls back to keychain-stored `google_client_id` /
# `google_client_secret` (handy for local dev).

ALFRED_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
ALFRED_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
